//! Center-origin, Y-up cameras for `Sprite` scenes.

/// An opaque 2D camera description.
type t = host

/// Create a camera with the visible world width and height at zoom 1.
///
/// The renderer preserves this aspect ratio and letterboxes rather than
/// stretching. Width and height must be positive.
let create : (float, float) => t

/// Center a camera at the given world position; the camera is last for piping.
let at : (float, float, t) => t
/// Set a positive camera zoom; the camera is last for piping.
///
/// LARGER is closer: the zoom divides the visible world extent, so `2.0` shows
/// half as much world at twice the size.
let zoom : (float, t) => t

/// Map a sampled mouse position through the camera's fitted viewport.
///
/// Returns `Option.None` while the pointer is in a letterbox/pillarbox bar.
/// The mouse carries its logical surface extent, so this remains correct
/// across window resizes and Retina/device-pixel-ratio changes.
let toWorld : (Input.mouse, t) => Option.t<Input.point2>
